            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0460" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v01/pg391"/>

                <head>105. Memorandum From Secretary of Defense Weinberger to the President’s
                    Assistant for National Security Affairs (Clark)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d105-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1982-06-09">June 9, 1982</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Prevention of Accidental Outbreak of War</item>
                </list>
                <p>If, as I suspect, it proves to be not possible to insert the proposal on
                    prevention of accidental war into the President’s Bonn speech,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d105-f2"/> I would suggest that the UN Special Session on
                    Disarmament would offer a particularly good and appropriate time to make the
                        point.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d105-f3"/></p>
                <p>Again, simply to summarize points I have previously made, there would be a strong
                    element of a new, easily understood, basically simple proposal, about which
                    there should be a very wide measure of agreement on all sides. Too, the
                    President would thus certainly appear to have taken the initiative to develop a
                    particular, constructive, and affirmative suggestion, whereas the rest of the
                    meeting will be the usual bloodbath of rhetoric out of which very little is
                    expected to emerge.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Cap</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d105-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d105-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Reagan Library, Executive Secretariat, NSC Agency File, Department of
                    Defense (05/06/1982–06/10/1982); NLR–747–2–29–11–3. Secret; Eyes Only. A stamped
                    notation in the top right-hand corner of the memorandum indicates that Clark saw
                    it. Another stamped notation indicates that it was received at 2:36 p.m. on June
                    10. Poindexter initialed another copy of the memorandum, on which an unknown
                    hand wrote: “6/11 Staff: Blair—per WC. Darman read memo. Indicated already being
                    done.” (Ibid.)</p>
            </note>
